<title>USA: McGraw-Hill to stay in NYC, keep over 4,000 jobs.</title>
<headline>McGraw-Hill to stay in NYC, keep over 4,000 jobs.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>McGraw-Hill Cos Inc announced with New York City and New York State officials that it would keep over 4,000 jobs in the city, including the company's Standard and Poor's Corp division.</p>
<p>Standard and Poor's had been negotiating with New Jersey officials, who were trying to lure it to a new office tower in Jersey City.</p>
